{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:computed-classification", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:residual-judgment", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:owner-ruling", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "C records reproducible facts and sufficient declared rule application; J records only unresolved semantics or materiality; O remains a ruling of its actual owner. None creates operation, admission or decision authority or a new calculus kind.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#computed-classification-and-treatment", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity"], "statement": "C records reproducible facts and sufficient declared rule application; J records only unresolved semantics or materiality; O remains a ruling of its actual owner. None creates operation, admission or decision authority or a new calculus kind.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:computed-facts-judgments-and-rulings-retain-owners"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:computed-classification", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:closed-frame-result", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "Each admission owner remains independently responsible for deriving and validating its complete enclosing relation. It may consume established facts whose exact subject, basis, scope, provenance and validity remain applicable, with recoverable production and invalidation. A function, component, role, conversation or status boundary alone requires no repeated derivation. Unsupported assertions of prior success establish nothing. Material mutation, rollback, changed authority or basis, expired validity and actual trust crossings require applicable validation before reliance or effect. Reuse transfers no admission responsibility, omits no participant and supplies no separately required independent judgment. All participants and joins remain bound to one admission-valid basis or declared coherent composite basis through one all-or-none semantic commit; if support can advance, revalidate or use a design-declared concurrency mechanism.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:computed-facts-judgments-and-rulings-retain-owners", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:support"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:closed-result-reuse-preserves-required-independence", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:support"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#complete-enclosing-relation-admission-stdo-up-021"], "statement": "Each admission owner remains independently responsible for deriving and validating its complete enclosing relation. It may consume established facts whose exact subject, basis, scope, provenance and validity remain applicable, with recoverable production and invalidation. A function, component, role, conversation or status boundary alone requires no repeated derivation. Unsupported assertions of prior success establish nothing. Material mutation, rollback, changed authority or basis, expired validity and actual trust crossings require applicable validation before reliance or effect. Reuse transfers no admission responsibility, omits no participant and supplies no separately required independent judgment. All participants and joins remain bound to one admission-valid basis or declared coherent composite basis through one all-or-none semantic commit; if support can advance, revalidate or use a design-declared concurrency mechanism.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:enclosing-admission-reuses-valid-established-facts"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:design", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "A finding or acceptance predicate binds a violated obligation, supported input or state, governing operating/threat model and credible causal path. An excluded threat alone authorizes neither a predicate nor retained defensive work; existing tests and hypothetical hostility supply no standing. Exclusion itself requires the governing owner, not a helper's inability to construct a case, and internal location alone establishes no trust. Preserve supported malformed-input, mutable-state, authority, freshness and effect checks. Audit affected predicates when replacing the responsibility; retire unsupported expectations without inventing a replacement guard. Live authority conflicts or a proposed wider model re-enter their actual owner rather than receiving a test-only waiver.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#standing-structural-qualification", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#derived-reviewer-frame", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#test-case-authority"], "statement": "A finding or acceptance predicate binds a violated obligation, supported input or state, governing operating/threat model and credible causal path. An excluded threat alone authorizes neither a predicate nor retained defensive work; existing tests and hypothetical hostility supply no standing. Exclusion itself requires the governing owner, not a helper's inability to construct a case, and internal location alone establishes no trust. Preserve supported malformed-input, mutable-state, authority, freshness and effect checks. Audit affected predicates when replacing the responsibility; retire unsupported expectations without inventing a replacement guard. Live authority conflicts or a proposed wider model re-enter their actual owner rather than receiving a test-only waiver.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:findings-and-tests-require-supported-operating-model"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:frame-applicability", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:closed-frame-result", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "Owning evaluation/scope predicates select obligations for the exact subject. True requires its evaluation and exact result; false excludes only that obligation under cited authority. Missing or ambiguous premises leave applicability unknown, never false. Available tools, frame names or families activate nothing by themselves; residual semantic applicability remains supported J.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#applicability-and-required-results"], "statement": "Owning evaluation/scope predicates select obligations for the exact subject. True requires its evaluation and exact result; false excludes only that obligation under cited authority. Missing or ambiguous premises leave applicability unknown, never false. Available tools, frame names or families activate nothing by themselves; residual semantic applicability remains supported J.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:frame-applicability-preserves-true-false-and-unknown"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:identity", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:public-serialization", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:work-outcome", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "Across serialization, parsing, normalization and adaptation, preserve domain, units, identity, cardinality, order, empty/null/default meaning and lifecycle validity. A lawful translation binds source/target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, owner and refusal. Distinguish proposed, admitted, assessed and completed states, active input from history, and current validity from available bytes. Equal wire shape or output proves neither translation nor equal meaning, provenance or authority.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#derived-end-to-end-interface-integration-frame", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#interface-integration-obligations"], "statement": "Across serialization, parsing, normalization and adaptation, preserve domain, units, identity, cardinality, order, empty/null/default meaning and lifecycle validity. A lawful translation binds source/target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, owner and refusal. Distinguish proposed, admitted, assessed and completed states, active input from history, and current validity from available bytes. Equal wire shape or output proves neither translation nor equal meaning, provenance or authority.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:interface-boundaries-preserve-domain-and-temporal-meaning"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:observed-effect-state", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "Preserve the supported originating causal frontier through wrappers and projections: material seam, bounded field/path, expected domain or basis, observed mismatch and evidence locator where available, together with downstream symptoms, successful work and declared continuation or block. Clock or log order alone identifies no cause. Preserve joint causes, alternative frontiers and indeterminacy instead of inventing a unique cause; honor Product redaction and name required diagnostic gaps. Return the smallest supported owner/re-entry without granting repair or retry.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#counterexample-localization", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#interface-integration-obligations"], "statement": "Preserve the supported originating causal frontier through wrappers and projections: material seam, bounded field/path, expected domain or basis, observed mismatch and evidence locator where available, together with downstream symptoms, successful work and declared continuation or block. Clock or log order alone identifies no cause. Preserve joint causes, alternative frontiers and indeterminacy instead of inventing a unique cause; honor Product redaction and name required diagnostic gaps. Return the smallest supported owner/re-entry without granting repair or retry.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:interface-causal-diagnostics-retain-frontier-and-uncertainty"}
{"arguments": [{"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:work-outcome", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:subject"}, {"literal": "At each material interface, bind input domain, producer guarantees, consumer preconditions, permitted effects, refusals and observable exit. A direct successful handoff meets consumer preconditions; candidate output, later admission and semantic assessment remain distinct when that is the declared contract. Refusal of an inadmissible candidate does not alone falsify an adequate candidate interface. Supply material actor obligations and domains in the actual context or through an exact lawfully accessible locator, including material LLM role, instructions, tools and transport/model configuration. Generic governance access cannot replace the Product contract or license hidden-validator inference. Deterministic owners expose their owned facts through reuse or equivalent projections; semantic judgment and reserved owner admission remain separately owned.", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:requirement"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:enclosing-admission-reuses-valid-established-facts", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:support"}, {"ref": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:computed-facts-judgments-and-rulings-retain-owners", "role": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:role:support"}], "clause_type": "constraint", "operator": "urn:stdo-representation:vocabulary:operator:requires", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#interface-integration-obligations"], "statement": "At each material interface, bind input domain, producer guarantees, consumer preconditions, permitted effects, refusals and observable exit. A direct successful handoff meets consumer preconditions; candidate output, later admission and semantic assessment remain distinct when that is the declared contract. Refusal of an inadmissible candidate does not alone falsify an adequate candidate interface. Supply material actor obligations and domains in the actual context or through an exact lawfully accessible locator, including material LLM role, instructions, tools and transport/model configuration. Generic governance access cannot replace the Product contract or license hidden-validator inference. Deterministic owners expose their owned facts through reuse or equivalent projections; semantic judgment and reserved owner admission remain separately owned.", "uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:interface-contract-exposes-domains-and-owned-facts"}
